{
 "_doc": "Brand registry for automatic logos (scripts/brands.py detects, scripts/brand_logo.py fetches into assets/brand/<slug>/). Keys = slug. aliases are matched case/diacritic-insensitively on word boundaries in narration + on-screen text. case:true = only when written with a capital first letter (common words: Threads, Make, Go, Medium). ctx:'social' = only when the same sentence/label also names another social platform (single letter X). Policy (Dan, 18 Oct 2026): every tech logo that can be found is shown; there is no trademark skip list. logo:false (+why) is only for a brand Dan explicitly turns off. attrib = credit line required by the logo licence (CC BY), printed on the end card. commons = explicit Wikimedia Commons file titles to try. si = Simple Icons slug, homepage/github = where the fetcher looks when Simple Icons has no icon. wordmark = quality skip: the only official mark is the name in type (macOS, iOS).  official = direct URL of the owner's brand asset, tried before Simple Icons (when Simple Icons has an outdated mark).",
